per's ghczuwrapper... name), the program's own code's"] [286 15 "// a safe (or interruptible) call: in the threaded way it releases the capability (threaded.go)"] [291 2 "// the void arguments (the State# token) are not C's"] [304 5 "// a capi import's wrapper, which the module's stubs define (a value of a header's macro: capi_value)"] [311 3 "// a function of the program's own C"] [340 4 "// an Array# or ArrayArray# argument (UnliftedFFITypes, T16650): its elements as C sees GHC's, a word each,"] [341 4 "// an object's identity (a pinned byte array its address; anything else an address of its own, made once)"] [383 1 "// convRes is a C result in its representation."] [406 1 "// CaseE is a case: its scrutinee evaluated under a case frame, then an alternative chosen."] [414 2 "// the alternatives indexed (HE4d): byTag by a constructor's tag once their constructors are loaded, byInt"] [415 2 "// by an integer literal's value; made at the case's first use with enough alternatives"] [419 2 "// k: the continuation compiled to Go (aot.go), when the case's closure was compiled ahead of time"] [423 1 "// index makes the case's tables (a case of four alternatives or more)."] [430 22 "// a constructor not loaded yet: again at the next use"] [500 1 "// cont chooses the alternative for the value in the return registers. A case of an algebraic type with a"] [501 1 "// default alone may see a function: a class of one method's dictionary is the method itself (a newtype)."] [533 4 "// a class of one method's dictionary is the method itself (a newtype): a default only"] [589 1 "// LetE allocates closures and constructors."] [602 14 "// staticCon"] [605 1 "// allocClosure is a closure of l with n free variables to fill: a function or a thunk, and its free slice."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[48 24] [58 48] [70 26] [326 37] [333 48] [339 27] [353 30] [453 21] [478 31] [487 25] [540 20] [541 23] [568 22]]} (go/file "nodes.go" :imports [


